---
import PreviewLayout from '../layouts/PreviewLayout.astro';
---

<PreviewLayout title="Signal — Separate work. One terminal." theme="signal" description="Crit is a worktree-first terminal workspace for OMP, OpenCode, and shells. Separate branches. Keep your context.">
  <div class="signal-page">
    <header class="masthead wrap">
      <a class="wordmark" href="#main" aria-label="Crit home"><span class="brand-mark" aria-hidden="true"><i></i><i></i><i></i></span>crit<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a>
      <nav aria-label="Main navigation"><a href="#workflow">The workflow</a><a href="#under-the-hood">Under the hood</a><a class="nav-start" href="#start">Start building <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></nav>
    </header>

    <main id="main">
      <section class="hero wrap" aria-labelledby="hero-title">
        <div class="hero-copy">
          <p class="eyebrow"><span class="signal-dot"></span> WORKTREE-FIRST TERMINAL WORKSPACE</p>
          <h1 id="hero-title">Separate<br />work.<br /><span>One terminal.</span></h1>
          <p class="hero-description">A place for every branch. A shell for every idea.<br class="desktop-break" /> Bring your agents and your worktrees together—without mixing them up.</p>
          <div class="hero-actions"><a class="primary-button" href="#start">Get started <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href="#workspace">Explore the workspace <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a></div>
          <p class="hero-fine">OMP / OPENCODE / YOUR SHELL <span>APACHE-2.0</span></p>
        </div>

        <div class="hero-instrument" id="workspace">
          <div class="instrument-caption"><span>FIG. 01 / WORKSPACE</span><span>INTERACTIVE ILLUSTRATION</span></div>
          <div class="workspace-console">
            <div class="console-toolbar"><span class="console-brand">crit <span id="workspace-path">atlas / feat-auth</span></span><span class="toolbar-status"><span class="signal-dot"></span> 3 WORKTREES</span></div>
            <div class="project-bar"><span class="project-active">atlas</span><span class="project-quiet">website</span><span class="project-quiet">sdk</span><span class="project-label">PROJECTS</span></div>
            <div class="console-body">
              <div class="worktree-list" role="group" aria-label="Choose illustrative worktree">
                <span class="list-label">WORKTREES</span>
                <button type="button" class="branch-option selected" data-branch="auth" aria-pressed="true"><span class="branch-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⑂</span><span><strong>feat/auth</strong><small>OMP + shell</small></span><span class="branch-indicator"></span></button>
                <button type="button" class="branch-option" data-branch="api" aria-pressed="false"><span class="branch-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⑂</span><span><strong>fix/api</strong><small>OpenCode + shell</small></span><span class="branch-indicator"></span></button>
                <button type="button" class="branch-option" data-branch="main" aria-pressed="false"><span class="branch-symbol" aria-hidden="true">⑂</span><span><strong>main</strong><small>Shell</small></span><span class="branch-indicator"></span></button>
                <div class="tree-foot"><span class="tree-lines" aria-hidden="true">└─</span> one branch<br />&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;one worktree</div>
              </div>
              <div class="panes">
                <div class="agent-pane focused" data-pane="agent">
                  <div class="pane-heading"><span id="agent-name">OMP</span><span class="pane-state" id="agent-state">AGENT SESSION</span></div>
                  <div class="agent-content"><p class="terminal-muted" id="agent-location">~/atlas/feat-auth</p><p class="terminal-prompt" id="agent-request"><span>›</span> Add session authentication</p><p id="agent-output">Reviewing the existing auth flow.<br />Working in <span class="terminal-lime">feat/auth</span>.</p><div class="agent-steps" id="agent-steps"><span>↳ src/auth/session.ts</span><span>↳ src/routes/login.ts</span></div><p class="agent-ready"><span class="signal-dot"></span><span id="agent-ready">Agent session open</span></p></div>
                </div>
                <div class="shell-pane" data-pane="shell">
                  <div class="pane-heading"><span>SHELL</span><span class="shell-path" id="shell-branch">feat/auth</span></div>
                  <div class="shell-content"><p><span class="terminal-lime">❯</span> <span id="shell-command">git status --short</span></p><p class="terminal-muted" id="shell-output">M src/auth/session.ts<br /> M src/routes/login.ts</p><p class="shell-cursor"><span class="terminal-lime">❯</span> <span class="cursor" aria-hidden="true"></span></p></div>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="demo-controls"><button type="button" id="focus-shell"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><span>+</span><kbd>D</kbd><span class="demo-button-label">Focus the shell</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></button><p id="demo-status" aria-live="polite">Select a branch. Keep the contexts separate.</p></div>
          <div class="instrument-coordinate" aria-hidden="true">BRANCH ≠ CONTEXT SWITCH</div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <div class="compatibility wrap"><p>YOUR TOOLS.<br /><strong>MORE ROOM TO WORK.</strong></p><div><span>OMP</span><span>OpenCode</span><span class="shell-tool"><span aria-hidden="true">›_</span> Shells</span><span class="git-tool"><span aria-hidden="true">⑂</span> Git worktrees</span></div><span class="compatibility-note">Not another coding agent.<br />The workspace around yours.</span></div>

      <section class="workflow wrap section" id="workflow" aria-labelledby="workflow-title">
        <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / KEEP YOUR CONTEXT</p><h2 id="workflow-title">More than one task.<br /><span>Less than one mess.</span></h2><p>Give parallel work a place of its own. Move between branches, agents, and shells without turning your terminal into a guessing game.</p></div>
        <div class="workflow-rows">
          <article><span class="step-number">01</span><div><h3>Branch out. Literally.</h3><p>Each branch gets a Git worktree. Your files live in separate working directories, with project tabs and split worktrees to keep the bigger picture in view.</p></div><span class="row-art branch-art" aria-hidden="true">main <i>┬── feat/auth</i><i>└── fix/api</i></span></article>
          <article><span class="step-number">02</span><div><h3>Close one tier at a time.</h3><p>Ctrl+D goes to whatever has focus, as in Kitty: the agent quits on it and its pane closes, a split’s survivor goes full width, an empty tab closes. Ctrl+Shift+Enter opens a shell beside the agent, which stays alive.</p></div><span class="row-art key-art" aria-hidden="true"><kbd>Ctrl</kbd><span>+</span><kbd>D</kbd></span></article>
          <article><span class="step-number">03</span><div><h3>Pick up where you left it.</h3><p>Switch projects without closing their sessions. Exit, then reopen Crit: your saved workspace and the same OMP/OpenCode chats return. Shells start fresh; old processes do not survive.</p></div><span class="row-art session-art" aria-hidden="true"><i></i> SAME CHAT</span></article>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="infrastructure" id="under-the-hood" aria-labelledby="infra-title">
        <div class="wrap infrastructure-grid">
          <div class="infra-copy"><p class="eyebrow">02 / SEPARATION, ALL THE WAY DOWN</p><h2 id="infra-title">Same project.<br /><span>Different moving parts.</span></h2><p>Optionally give each worktree its own Docker Compose project, networks, named volumes, and dynamic loopback ports.</p><p class="infra-note">Local development separation—not a security sandbox. Configured bind mounts can still share data. Exiting Crit does not stop your Docker stacks.</p></div>
          <div class="compose-diagram" aria-label="Illustration of separate Compose resources for two worktrees"><div class="diagram-title"><span>OPTIONAL / DOCKER COMPOSE</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><div class="compose-lane"><div class="lane-branch"><span aria-hidden="true">⑂</span> feat/auth</div><div class="lane-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="resource-group"><span>COMPOSE PROJECT A</span><p><i></i> Network A</p><p><i></i> Named volume A</p><p class="port">127.0.0.1:<b>49152</b></p></div></div><div class="compose-lane"><div class="lane-branch"><span aria-hidden="true">⑂</span> fix/api</div><div class="lane-connector" aria-hidden="true"></div><div class="resource-group"><span>COMPOSE PROJECT B</span><p><i></i> Network B</p><p><i></i> Named volume B</p><p class="port">127.0.0.1:<b>49153</b></p></div></div><p class="diagram-caption">Illustrative resources and port assignments</p></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <section class="controls-section wrap section" aria-labelledby="controls-title"><div><p class="eyebrow">03 / TWO WAYS IN</p><h2 id="controls-title">Ask naturally.<br /><span>Or take the controls.</span></h2></div><div class="control-options"><article><kbd>F1</kbd><div><h3>Ask Crit</h3><p>Use the natural-language launcher to tell Crit what you need. Requires authenticated OMP.</p></div></article><article><kbd>F2</kbd><div><h3>Manual controls</h3><p>Prefer the direct route? Open the manual controls. No natural-language launcher required.</p></div></article></div></section>

      <section class="start-section wrap" id="start" aria-labelledby="start-title"><div class="start-copy"><p class="eyebrow">04 / MAKE ROOM</p><h2 id="start-title">Your next branch<br />starts here<span>.</span></h2><p>Open source. Apache-2.0.<br />Built for the work already on your terminal.</p></div><div class="install-panel"><div class="install-header"><span>BUILD FROM SOURCE</span><button type="button" id="copy-install">Copy commands <span aria-hidden="true">⧉</span></button></div><p class="install-context">From the root of a local Crit checkout:</p><pre><code id="install-commands">cargo install --path .
crit</code></pre><p class="install-requirements">You’ll need <strong>Rust / Cargo</strong> and <strong>Git</strong>. Have OMP or OpenCode available when you use them. Docker Compose is optional.</p><details><summary>Using Kitty? <span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div><p>For optional Kitty integration, run:</p><code>crit setup kitty</code><p>Then reload your Kitty configuration.</p></div></details><p class="copy-status" id="copy-status" aria-live="polite">Two commands. Your own local checkout.</p></div></section>
    </main>
    <footer class="wrap footer"><a class="wordmark" href="#main">crit<span class="wordmark-dot">.</span></a><p>Separate work. Stay in your flow.</p><a href="#start">Build from source <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><span>CONCEPT 01 / SIGNAL</span></footer>
  </div>
</PreviewLayout>

<script>
  const examples = {
    auth: { branch: 'feat/auth', path: 'feat-auth', agent: 'OMP', request: 'Add session authentication', output: 'Reviewing the existing auth flow.', files: ['src/auth/session.ts', 'src/routes/login.ts'], command: 'git status --short', shell: ' M src/auth/session.ts\n M src/routes/login.ts' },
    api: { branch: 'fix/api', path: 'fix-api', agent: 'OPENCODE', request: 'Fix response pagination', output: 'Tracing the pagination boundary.', files: ['src/api/list.ts', 'src/api/pagination.ts'], command: 'git diff --stat', shell: ' src/api/list.ts       | 8 +++++---\n src/api/pagination.ts | 6 ++++--' },
    main: { branch: 'main', path: 'main', agent: 'NO AGENT', request: 'A clean starting point', output: 'This worktree has a shell, no agent.', files: ['Working tree clean', 'Ready for your next task'], command: 'git status --short', shell: 'Working tree clean' },
  };
  let selected: keyof typeof examples = 'auth';
  let shellFocused = false;
  const text = (id: string, value: string) => { const el = document.getElementById(id); if (el) el.textContent = value; };
  function updateFocus() {
    document.querySelector('[data-pane="agent"]')?.classList.toggle('focused', !shellFocused);
    document.querySelector('[data-pane="shell"]')?.classList.toggle('focused', shellFocused);
    text('agent-state', selected === 'main' ? 'NO SESSION' : shellFocused ? 'STILL OPEN' : 'AGENT SESSION');
    const label = document.querySelector('#focus-shell .demo-button-label');
    if (label) label.textContent = shellFocused ? 'Shell selected' : 'Focus the shell';
    const button = document.getElementById('focus-shell') as HTMLButtonElement | null;
    if (button) button.disabled = shellFocused;
  }
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-branch]').forEach(button => {
    button.addEventListener('click', () => {
      const key = button.dataset.branch as keyof typeof examples;
      const example = examples[key];
      if (!example) return;
      selected = key;
      shellFocused = key === 'main';
      document.querySelectorAll('[data-branch]').forEach(option => {
        const active = option === button;
        option.classList.toggle('selected', active);
        option.setAttribute('aria-pressed', String(active));
      });
      text('agent-name', example.agent);
      text('agent-location', `~/atlas/${example.path}`);
      text('agent-request', `› ${example.request}`);
      text('agent-output', `${example.output}\nWorking in ${example.branch}.`);
      const steps = document.getElementById('agent-steps');
      if (steps) steps.replaceChildren(...example.files.map(file => { const span = document.createElement('span'); span.textContent = `↳ ${file}`; return span; }));
      text('agent-ready', key === 'main' ? 'Shell-only worktree' : 'Agent session open');
      text('shell-branch', example.branch);
      text('shell-command', example.command);
      text('shell-output', example.shell);
      text('workspace-path', `atlas / ${example.path}`);
      text('demo-status', `${example.branch} selected. ${key === 'main' ? 'A clean shell-only workspace.' : `${example.agent} and shell have their own context.`}`);
      updateFocus();
    });
  });
  document.getElementById('focus-shell')?.addEventListener('click', () => {
    shellFocused = true;
    updateFocus();
    text('demo-status', 'Shell focused. The agent session stays open.');
  });
  document.getElementById('copy-install')?.addEventListener('click', async () => {
    try {
      if (!navigator.clipboard) throw new Error('Clipboard unavailable');
      await navigator.clipboard.writeText('cargo install --path .\ncrit');
      text('copy-status', 'Copied. Run these from your local Crit checkout.');
    } catch {
      text('copy-status', 'Clipboard unavailable. Select and copy the commands above.');
    }
  });
</script>

<style>
  :global(body[data-concept='signal']) { background: #10120f; color: #e8eae3; }
  .signal-page { --lime: #c6f36b; --muted: #969d91; --line: #30362c; background: #10120f; color: #e8eae3; overflow: hidden; padding-bottom: 80px; }
  .wrap { width: min(1392px, calc(100% - 112px)); margin-inline: auto; }
  a { color: inherit; text-decoration: none; }
  .masthead { height: 104px; display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .wordmark { font: 700 37px/1 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -2px; display: inline-flex; align-items: center; }
  .wordmark-dot { color: var(--lime); }
  .brand-mark { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 3px; margin-right: 14px; }
  .brand-mark i { background: var(--lime); width: 5px; height: 24px; transform: skewY(-28deg); }
  .brand-mark i:nth-child(2) { height: 33px; }
  nav { display: flex; gap: 34px; align-items: center; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 500; }
  nav a { color: #b6bbae; transition: color .2s; }
  nav a:hover, .text-link:hover { color: var(--lime); }
  .nav-start { color: #e8eae3; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); padding-left: 34px; }
  .nav-start span { margin-left: 20px; color: var(--lime); }
  .hero { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1.05fr; gap: 42px; padding-top: 81px; padding-bottom: 76px; align-items: center; }
  .eyebrow { font: 10px/1.6 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 1.25px; color: var(--muted); margin: 0 0 30px; }
  .hero .eyebrow { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 9px; white-space: nowrap; }
  .signal-dot { width: 5px; height: 5px; background: var(--lime); display: inline-block; flex-shrink: 0; border-radius: 50%; }
  h1 { margin: 0; font: 500 clamp(65px, 6.7vw, 104px)/.98 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -.065em; }
  h1 > span { color: var(--lime); white-space: nowrap; }
  .hero-description { font-size: 14px; line-height: 1.9; color: #b3b9aa; margin: 31px 0 27px; max-width: 380px; }
  .hero-actions { display: flex; gap: 24px; align-items: center; }
  .primary-button { background: var(--lime); color: #171d10; padding: 15px 20px; font-size: 12px; font-weight: 650; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 37px; transition: background .2s; }
  .primary-button:hover { background: #d8ff94; }
  .text-link { font-size: 11px; display: flex; gap: 13px; align-items: center; }
  .hero-fine { font: 10px/1.6 var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: .65px; color: #8a937e; margin-top: 29px; display: flex; gap: 20px; }
  .hero-fine span { border-left: 1px solid var(--line); padding-left: 20px; }
  .hero-instrument { position: relative; min-width: 0; padding-top: 16px; }
  .hero-instrument::before { content: ''; position: absolute; inset: -38px -34px -49px -34px; background-image: linear-gradient(#20251c 1px, transparent 1px), linear-gradient(90deg, #20251c 1px, transparent 1px); background-size: 32px 32px; opacity: .55; mask-image: linear-gradient(90deg, transparent, #000 20%, #000 80%, transparent); pointer-events: none; }
  .instrument-caption { position: relative; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; font: 8px var(--font-mono); letter-spacing: 1px; color: #7f8975; margin: 0 0 13px; }
  .workspace-console { position: relative; background: #171b14; border: 1px solid #46513b; box-shadow: 0 20px 50px #0005, 7px 7px 0 #1d2318, 8px 8px 0 #313a27; border-radius: 4px; font-family: var(--font-mono); overflow: hidden; }
  .console-toolbar { display: flex; align-items: center; justify-content: space-between; height: 47px; padding: 0 16px; background: #242a1e; border-bottom: 1px solid #39422e; }
  .console-brand { font-size: 14px; font-weight: 600; color: var(--lime); }
  .console-brand span { font-size: 10px; color: #a0aa94; font-weight: 400; margin-left: 7px; }
  .toolbar-status { font-size: 7px; letter-spacing: .8px; color: #a2ac95; display: flex; gap: 7px; align-items: center; }
  .project-bar { height: 39px; display: flex; align-items: stretch; border-bottom: 1px solid #323a2b; gap: 0; font-size: 9px; }
  .project-bar > span:not(.project-label) { padding: 13px 19px; }
  .project-active { color: var(--lime); border-bottom: 2px solid var(--lime); background: #c6f36b08; }
  .project-quiet { color: #7b8570; }
  .project-label { margin-left: auto; padding: 15px 13px; font-size: 9px; color: #8e9c80; letter-spacing: 1px; }
  .console-body { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 142px 1fr; min-height: 359px; }
  .worktree-list { border-right: 1px solid #343d2b; background: #191f15; padding-top: 18px; }
  .list-label { font-size: 7px; letter-spacing: 1px; color: #89957c; display: block; margin: 0 14px 14px; }
  .branch-option { display: flex; text-align: left; align-items: center; gap: 8px; padding: 12px 11px; width: 100%; color: #9fa991; border: 0; border-left: 2px solid transparent; background: transparent; cursor: pointer; font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .branch-option:hover { background: #252e1e; }
  .branch-option.selected { background: #c6f36b0c; border-left-color: var(--lime); color: var(--lime); }
  .branch-symbol { font-size: 20px; }
  .branch-option strong { display: block; font-size: 9px; font-weight: 400; }
  .branch-option small { display: block; font-size: 7px; color: #879579; margin-top: 5px; }
  .branch-indicator { width: 4px; height: 4px; border-radius: 50%; background: #5f6e52; margin-left: auto; }
  .selected .branch-indicator { background: var(--lime); }
  .tree-foot { border-top: 1px solid #303926; margin: 43px 13px 0; padding-top: 18px; font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.8; color: #8e9c80; }
  .tree-lines { color: var(--lime); }
  .panes { min-width: 0; padding: 8px; display: grid; grid-template-rows: 1fr 130px; gap: 7px; }
  .agent-pane, .shell-pane { border: 1px solid #34412a; background: #11160e; min-width: 0; transition: border-color .2s, background .2s; }
  .focused { border-color: #9ac850; background: #151c10; }
  .pane-heading { display: flex; justify-content: space-between; background: #1e2718; border-bottom: 1px solid #303d25; padding: 9px 10px; font-size: 8px; color: #adbba0; letter-spacing: .8px; gap: 6px; }
  .focused .pane-heading { color: var(--lime); background: #27351c; }
  .pane-state, .shell-path { font-size: 9px; color: #a2b18f; }
  .agent-content { padding: 12px; font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.8; color: #bec8b4; }
  .agent-content p { margin: 0 0 12px; white-space: pre-line; }
  .terminal-muted { color: #7d8c70; }
  .terminal-prompt { color: #e0e8d5; }
  .terminal-prompt span { color: var(--lime); margin-right: 6px; }
  .terminal-lime { color: var(--lime); }
  .agent-steps { display: grid; color: #899a79; margin-bottom: 13px; }
  .agent-content .agent-ready { margin: 0; font-size: 7px; color: #93a783; display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 6px; }
  .shell-content { padding: 9px 11px; font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.7; }
  .shell-content p { margin: 0 0 4px; white-space: pre; }
  .cursor { display: inline-block; width: 6px; height: 10px; background: #d1ddc2; vertical-align: -1px; }
  .demo-controls { position: relative; display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; gap: 17px; padding-top: 21px; }
  .demo-controls button { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 5px; font: 8px var(--font-mono); color: #c8d3bc; border: 0; background: transparent; padding: 0; cursor: pointer; white-space: nowrap; }
  .demo-controls button:disabled { cursor: default; opacity: .55; }
  kbd { font-family: var(--font-mono); }
  .demo-controls kbd { border: 1px solid #48543c; padding: 4px; border-radius: 3px; }
  .demo-button-label { margin-left: 5px; }
  .demo-controls p { font: 8px/1.7 var(--font-mono); color: #859479; text-align: right; margin: 0; max-width: 170px; }
  .instrument-coordinate { position: relative; font: 9px var(--font-mono); color: #8a937e; letter-spacing: 1px; margin-top: 21px; text-align: right; }
  .compatibility { padding: 29px 0; display: flex; align-items: center; border-block: 1px solid var(--line); gap: 44px; }
  .compatibility > p { font: 8px/1.8 var(--font-mono); color: #8b9382; margin: 0; min-width: 140px; letter-spacing: .5px; }
  .compatibility strong { color: #bec6b4; font-weight: 400; }
  .compatibility > div { flex: 1; display: flex; justify-content: space-around; gap: 25px; align-items: center; color: #c1c7b9; font: 500 19px var(--font-display); }
  .shell-tool { font-family: var(--font-mono); font-size: 16px; }
  .shell-tool > span, .git-tool > span { color: #79876b; margin-right: 4px; }
  .compatibility-note { font-size: 9px; line-height: 1.7; color: #7e8874; border-left: 1px solid var(--line); padding-left: 29px; }
  .section { padding-block: 99px; }
  h2 { margin: 0; font: 500 44px/1.12 var(--font-display); letter-spacing: -2px; }
  h2 > span { color: #88967b; }
  .section-intro { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; column-gap: 80px; align-items: end; margin-bottom: 48px; }
  .section-intro .eyebrow { grid-column: 1 / -1; margin-bottom: 22px; }
  .section-intro > p:last-child { max-width: 330px; font-size: 12px; line-height: 1.9; color: #a1aa97; margin: 0 0 3px auto; }
  .workflow-rows { border-top: 1px solid var(--line); }
  .workflow-rows article { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 55px 1fr 210px; gap: 22px; align-items: center; padding: 30px 0; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); }
